<td id="S4.T1.2.16.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><math id="S4.T1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0221\pm 0.0007" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.0221</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.0007</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0221\pm 0.0007</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T1.2.16.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, <math id="S4.T1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}2</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.16.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><math id="S4.T1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.0006" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.0006</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.0006</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><math id="S4.T1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.2.17.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">object</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.17.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.2.17.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">RepViT</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.17.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><math id="S4.T1.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0357\pm 0.0118" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.0357</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.0118</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0357\pm 0.0118</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T1.2.17.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, <math id="S4.T1.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}2</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.17.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><math id="S4.T1.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.0142" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.0142</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.0142</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Per-(backbone, suite) encoder ranking under the fixed
grafting protocol. All numbers are under a unified <math id="S4.T1.m69" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224{\times}224" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>224</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>224</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224{\times}224</annotation></semantics></math>
preprocessing path; encoders may shift ranking under per-encoder
official preprocessing — see Limitations. Numbers are mean
validation MSE with cross-seed standard deviation and seed count
<math id="S4.T1.m70" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>; SigLIP and DINOv2 are reported at <math id="S4.T1.m71" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> seeds ({42, 43, 44})
while FastViT and RepViT are <math id="S4.T1.m72" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}2</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S4.T1.26" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exploratory</em> cells
({42, 43}) rather than confirmatory cells; the
load-bearing inferential summary is restricted to the
SigLIP-vs-DINOv2 contrast at <math id="S4.T1.m73" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="S4.T1.m74" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> vs best is the gap
to the per-cell winner. On
<math id="S4.T1.m75" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="S4.T1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">object</span>, the top three encoders sit within
<math id="S4.T1.m76" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.7\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.7</mn><mo mathsize="1.430em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.7\%</annotation></semantics></math> relative of each other, which we read as a near-tie band
rather than as a stable ranking. We additionally flag the
<math id="S4.T1.m77" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="S4.T1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">spatial</span>-seed-44 DINOv2-vs-SigLIP cell as a
numerical near-tie (<math id="S4.T1.m78" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=0.00001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=0.00001</annotation></semantics></math> MSE, <math id="S4.T1.m79" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.04\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.04</mn><mo mathsize="1.430em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.04\%</annotation></semantics></math> relative);
the <math id="S4.T1.m80" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="S4.T1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">spatial</span> suite-level direction is nominally
<math id="S4.T1.m81" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/3</annotation></semantics></math> DINOv2-winning, but the seed-44 cell is at the edge of
cross-seed noise rather than a substantive within-seed win.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.7 </span>Directional consistency and descriptive effect sizes</h3>

<div id="S4.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our load-bearing summary is the suite-level direction of the
SigLIP-vs-DINOv2 paired comparison across the four (backbone, suite)
cells. Three of the four backbone-suite directions support the
backbone-dependent top-tier pattern (SmolVLA favors SigLIP on both
suites; <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math> favors DINOv2 on <span id="S4.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">spatial</span>), with the lone
exception being <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="S4.SS7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">libero_object</span> where the
direction holds at only <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/3</annotation></semantics></math> seeds and seed-44 reverses. We report
this <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/4</annotation></semantics></math> suite-level summary as the
load-bearing inferential statement and deliberately do <em id="S4.SS7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em>
attach a sign-test <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value to it: the comparisons
share dataset, projector code, and seed schedule, so the
binomial-null calculation would be optimistic about independence.
At the finer cell level, SigLIP attains lower MSE than DINOv2 in all
<math id="S4.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6/6</annotation></semantics></math> SmolVLA (suite, seed) cells; on <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>, DINOv2 attains
lower MSE than SigLIP in <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5/6</annotation></semantics></math> (suite, seed) cells, with a single
seed-44 reversal on <span id="S4.SS7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">libero_object</span> (SigLIP <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.02018&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.02018</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.02018&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> DINOv2
<math id="S4.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.02288" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.02288</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.02288</annotation></semantics></math>). This <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11/12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11/12</annotation></semantics></math> vs <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/12</annotation></semantics></math> cell-level split is descriptive
evidence consistent with the suite-level statement; we report it for
reader transparency but treat it as descriptive rather than
independent inferential evidence, because the cells within a suite
share seeds, projector initialization, and validation episode order,
so they are not pseudo-independent samples (a naive two-sided sign
test against the <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50/50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50/50</annotation></semantics></math> null would imply <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\approx 0.006" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.006</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\approx 0.006</annotation></semantics></math>, but this
ignores the pseudo-replication structure and we therefore do not
defend the value). We additionally flag the seed-44 razor-thin
DINOv2-vs-SigLIP gap on <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>-<span id="S4.SS7.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">libero_spatial</span>
(<math id="S4.SS7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.02510" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.02510</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.02510</annotation></semantics></math> DINOv2 vs <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.02511" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.02511</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.02511</annotation></semantics></math> SigLIP, a <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.04\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.04</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.04\%</annotation></semantics></math> relative
near-tie, <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=0.00001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=0.00001</annotation></semantics></math> MSE) as evidence that the cross-encoder
gap on this slice is at the edge of cross-seed noise even when the
direction is preserved.</p>
</div>
